  <section class="faith-intro">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <details class="faith-intro-disclosure" data-faith-intro>
        <summary class="faith-intro-summary">
          <span class="faith-intro-summary-label" data-faith-intro-label>Read introduction</span>
          <span class="faith-intro-summary-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faith-intro-body">
          <p class="faith-intro-prose hero-excerpt-dropcap">The Thirty-Nine Articles of Religion were finalized in 1571 to define the doctrinal position of the Church of England between the Roman and Reformed extremes after the upheaval of the English Reformation. They are deliberately moderate and broadly Protestant - Reformed in their doctrine of grace, churchly in their sacramental theology, open enough to hold together a national church. They remain the doctrinal standard of the Anglican Communion.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
    
